# Security / CI / infrastructure changes

- Data stays local by default. Do not add SaaS SDKs, network egress, external error reporting, analytics, or remote caching without permission, privacy review and ADR.
- No credentials, tokens, DICOM, MRI, EEG, XDF, physiological data or identifying photos in Git, issues, screenshots or agent context. Use fake/synthetic fixtures only.
- CI gets read-only least-privilege token, pinned or reviewed actions and no secrets on untrusted PRs. Do not let agents weaken/change branch protections or governance checks to pass a build.
- Do not auto-install new system packages, perform major version upgrades, or use `curl | sh` in project scripts absent explicit human approval.
- Manage dependency updates separately; run lockfile checks and tests; security fixes should be focused and documented.
